The frontier is separating into *generative cognition* and *enforced
capability selection*. At the same time, tool markets make the capability
set dynamic and self-expanding. Therefore the scarce security primitive is
not prompt filtering. It is a continuously recomputed graph of what the
principal can now cause to happen.

The important state transition is:

authority_t + tool acquisition/payment + new runtime/network/credential
edges -> authority_(t+1)

A permission granted at t cannot be assumed safe at t+1 after the agent
buys, installs, discovers or composes a new capability. Privately should
treat capability acquisition as an authority-changing event requiring graph
recomputation.
