15. NON-OBVIOUS EDGE / SEESAW CONSEQUENCE
<p>The frontier is separating into <strong>generative cognition</strong> an=
d <strong>enforced capability selection</strong>. At the same time, tool ma=
rkets make the capability set dynamic and self-expanding. Therefore the sca=
rce security primitive is not prompt filtering. It is a continuously recomp=
uted graph of what the principal can now cause to happen.</p>
<p>The important state transition is:</p>
<p><code>authority_t + tool acquisition/payment + new runtime/network/crede=
ntial edges -&gt; authority_(t+1)</code></p>
<p>A permission granted at t cannot be assumed safe at t+1 after the agent =
buys, installs, discovers or composes a new capability. Privately should tr=
eat capability acquisition as an authority-changing event requiring graph r=
ecomputation.</p>

